      "text": "Latent growth curve modeling within a structural equation framework examined whether digital engagement moderates executive function decline beyond traditional cognitive reserve proxies. High engagement (≥3.5 hours/day of cognitively stimulating technology) attenuated decline by 58%, specifically in cognitive flexibility (β = 0.24) and planning (β = 0.21), whereas passive consumption showed no effect. Findings highlight that quality and type of digital activity, not screen time alone, influence cognitive aging trajectories.",
