      "text": "Problematic social media use (PSMU) has been increasingly associated with various psychological vulnerabilities; however, findings remain mixed, particularly among university students and in non-Western contexts. Participants completed a sociodemographic and clinical information form, the Social Media Addiction Scale-Adult Form, Adult Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder Self-Report Scale, Liebowitz Social Anxiety Scale, and Rosenberg Self-Esteem Scale-Short Form. The findings indicate that problematic social media use among university students is closely associated with psychological vulnerabilities, particularly ADHD symptoms and social anxiety, whereas the role of self-esteem appears more nuanced.",
      "paperTitle": "The relationship between problematic social media use and psychological factors among university students with evaluation of ADHD, social anxiety and self-esteem.",
      "doi": "10.1097/MD.0000000000050740",
      "source": "Medicine",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "This study aimed to examine the associations between PSMU and psychological factors including attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) symptoms, social anxiety, and self-esteem among university students, as well as to explore the role of selected sociodemographic and usage-related characteristics.",
      "paperTitle": "The relationship between problematic social media use and psychological factors among university students with evaluation of ADHD, social anxiety and self-esteem.",
      "doi": "10.1097/MD.0000000000050740",
      "source": "Medicine",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "This cross-sectional study included 179 university students aged 18 to 25 years.",
