    },
    {
      "text": "For individuals with obsessive-compulsive and related disorders (OCRDs) that are, in part, maintained by safety behaviors and other negative reinforcement loops, large language models (LLMs) can function as highly available, potentially sycophantic, and readily repeatable sources of reassurance that may undermine the principles of exposure and response prevention (ERP).",
      "paperTitle": "The Patient-AI Relationship in Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders: A Cognitive-Behavioral Framework.",
      "doi": "10.3390/jcm15187154",
      "source": "Journal of clinical medicine",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "Measurement paradigms inherited from the early digital era (e.g., screen time and problematic internet use) were not designed to capture these relational dynamics.",
      "paperTitle": "The Patient-AI Relationship in Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders: A Cognitive-Behavioral Framework.",
      "doi": "10.3390/jcm15187154",
      "source": "Journal of clinical medicine",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "We argue that generative AI may interfere with exposure-based treatment (by eroding therapeutic friction), the discomfort, delay, and uncertainty on which corrective learning depends.",
      "paperTitle": "The Patient-AI Relationship in Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders: A Cognitive-Behavioral Framework.",
      "doi": "10.3390/jcm15187154",
      "source": "Journal of clinical medicine",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "We suggest that this occurs through three interlocking mechanisms: supernormal stimuli, algorithmic sycophancy, and digital accommodation.",
      "paperTitle": "The Patient-AI Relationship in Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders: A Cognitive-Behavioral Framework.",
      "doi": "10.3390/jcm15187154",
      "source": "Journal of clinical medicine",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Adjunct ratings capture adaptive benefit, global interference, concealment, and safety-relevant exchanges.",
      "paperTitle": "The Patient-AI Relationship in Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders: A Cognitive-Behavioral Framework.",
      "doi": "10.3390/jcm15187154",
      "source": "Journal of clinical medicine",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Hypothesized digital phenotypes may be derived from the domain-level profiles.",
      "paperTitle": "The Patient-AI Relationship in Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders: A Cognitive-Behavioral Framework.",
      "doi": "10.3390/jcm15187154",
