  "10.2196/88572": [
    {
      "text": "Objective: The aim of this systematic review was to examine the association between PSU and ED psychopathology or ED-related outcomes (eg, body dissatisfaction, emotional eating, and food addiction) in clinical and nonclinical populations and explore potential moderators and mediators. Positive associations were also found across studies between PSU and several ED-related outcomes including food addiction, body dissatisfaction, uncontrolled eating, and emotional overeating. Conclusions: PSU and greater daily smartphone screen time are associated with higher ED symptoms, body image dissatisfaction, and broader disordered eating behaviors.",
      "paperTitle": "Associations of Problematic Smartphone Use and Smartphone Screen Time With Eating Disorder Psychopathology in Non-Clinical Samples: A Systematic Review",
      "doi": "10.2196/88572",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "Background: The ubiquitous use of smartphones has given rise to maladaptive patterns of use, often termed \"problematic smartphone use\" (PSU), which disproportionately impacts children and young people and is associated with poor mental health.",
