  "10.1080/2331186x.2026.2682595": [
    {
      "text": "The aim of this study was to describe the level of physical activity, sedentary time and screen use of schoolchildren, analyzing the existence of differences based on contextual factors and the level of weekly physical activity. Sedentary time during the school week is greater in the sixth grade of primary school (p < .05; r = 0.52) and on weekends when the mother performs work in the primary sector (p < .05; ε2 = 0.04). The mother’s modeling influences the amount of physical sports activity performed by the schoolchildren, as well as the type of work of the mother on the amount of sedentary time of the children.Impact statementThis research indicates that rural schoolchildren in Spain often exceed the recommended two-hour daily limit for screen-based leisure, with sixth-grade schoolchildren displaying higher levels of sedentary behavior compared to those in the fifth grade.",
      "paperTitle": "Screen time and physical activity in schoolchildren",
      "doi": "10.1080/2331186x.2026.2682595",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 0
    },
