    {
      "text": "Still, only 35.6% of children globally meet this guideline (McArthur et al., 2022).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 19
    },
    {
      "text": "This choice is guided by several considerations: First, preschool age is categorized by rapid cognitive development and high plasticity (Jin and Lin, 2022;Rueda et al., 2004).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "Several reviews adopt a broader age range of interest (e.g.,Kirkorian et al., 2024;Dewi et al., 2025;Anderson et al., 2017;Eirich et al., 2022;Santos et al., 2022).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 21
    },
    {
      "text": "(2024), it appears as one of the several thematic dimensions within reviews of language development and executive functions.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "While, as a mini-review, the present work does not provide an exhaustive analysis of the literature, the selected format enables a targeted examination of the studies addressing our research question within a rapidly evolving technological landscape.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 23
    },
    {
      "text": "Additionally, we explore mediating factors within these associations to elucidate the underlying mechanisms.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 24
    },
    {
      "text": "Ambiguous cases were re-evaluated against operational definitions using a decision rule, whereby classification was determined by the extent to which the activity required interaction between the child and the screen device used.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 25
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies were excluded if they only measured “total screen time” and therefore could not be placed within either category.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 26
    },
    {
      "text": "Coding was conducted by a single reviewer (seeSupplementary materialfor coding procedure).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 27
    },
    {
      "text": "To identify potentially relevant literature, the databases Google Scholar, PubMed, and PsychInfo were searched between February and October 2025.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 28
    },
    {
      "text": "This search strategy was supported by screening relevant review papers.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 29
    },
    {
      "text": "The full search strategy can be found in theSupplementary material.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "The review was restricted to children aged 3–5 years, and excluded those involving clinical populations (e.g., ADHD).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 31
    },
    {
      "text": "(2019)Top-down and bottom-up (dorsal/ventral networks)fMRI functional connectivityStory exposure (animated.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 32
    },
    {
      "text": "Illustrated, audio) during fMRIJin and Lin (2022)Alerting, orienting, executive attentionANT-C: reaction times and accuracyParent-reported weekly tablet useJourdren et al.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 33
    },
    {
      "text": "(2022)Selective, sustained, alternated, dividedSystematic review (varied tools)Systematic review (varied tools)Twait et al.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 34
    },
    {
      "text": "Complementary fMRI evidence fromHutton et al.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 35
    },
    {
      "text": "(2019)converge with behavioral findings fromAlmeida et al.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 36
    },
    {
      "text": "Moreover, animated stimuli may bias attention toward visual perception, likely motivating children to continue seeking animated screen content (Hutton et al., 2019).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 37
    },
    {
      "text": "In a similar study,Portugal et al.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "Additionally, long-term use was associated with slightly poorer endogenous attention control (Wald χ2= 3.95,p= 0.047).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 39
    },
    {
      "text": "However, there was no significant difference in comprehension.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 40
    },
    {
      "text": "Modern devices have the capacity to log activity-specific usage data.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 41
    },
    {
      "text": "Others have also critiqued this approach, arguing that it captures overt difficulties and likely neglects subtler or domain-specific variations in attentional control (Jourdren et al., 2023).",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 42
    },
    {
      "text": "Parent-reports offer valuable insights but are also subject to potential bias.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 43
    },
    {
      "text": "It should be noted that most studies employ cross-sectional or correlational designs, which preclude causal inferences.Jourdren et al.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 44
    },
    {
      "text": "Several mechanisms may explain this pattern.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 45
    },
    {
      "text": "Accordingly, the discussion of methodological strengths and limitations reflects interpretative comparison rather than systematic quality grading procedures typically employed in systematic reviews.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 46
    },
    {
      "text": "The present review did not differentiate between these potential subcategories.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 47
    },
    {
      "text": "Overall, the findings indicate that the passive-active distinction, as well as consideration of both the content and mode of engagement, may be theoretically useful.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 48
    },
    {
      "text": "More consistent operationalization across studies may facilitate interpretation and cross-study comparisons.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 49
    },
    {
      "text": "Future meta-analyses could provide a quantitative synthesis of the findings across studies.",
      "paperTitle": "Passive and active screen time relate differently to attention in preschool children",
      "doi": "10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1737937",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
