      "text": "Before proceeding to the main survey, all participants were presented with an informed consent statement at the beginning of the questionnaire. This statement outlined the purpose of the study, the voluntary nature of participation, anonymity of responses, and the confidential treatment of all data collected. Consent was obtained through a digital agreement checkbox, which participants had to tick before gaining access to the rest of the questionnaire. All participants were presented with a digital informed consent form embedded at the beginning of the online survey. This form provided comprehensive information regarding the purpose of the study, the nature of the questions, expected duration, confidentiality assurances, and the voluntary nature of their involvement. Participants had to indicate their agreement before proceeding with the questionnaire, and they could withdraw at any point without penalty. Prior to data collection, all participants received comprehensive information regarding the study’s purpose, procedures, potential risks and benefits, and their voluntary participation. Informed consent was obtained from all participants, with the assurance that they could withdraw at any time without penalty.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
