      "text": "Cases with significant missing data were excluded using listwise deletion, while normality was assessed using skewness and kurtosis values. Cases with significant missing data were excluded using listwise deletion49,50. The pattern of missingness was assessed using Little’s MCAR test, which indicated that the missing data were missing completely at random (MCAR; χ2= 12.37, df = 10,p= .26). Little’s MCAR test indicated that data were missing completely at random (χ2= 112.47, df = 105,p= .31), supporting the use of listwise deletion without introducing bias. To address this concern, we implemented a Holm–Bonferroni correction within families of related tests, thereby controlling the family-wise error rate at α = 0.05.",
