      "text": "Each section employed validated psychometric tools or adapted instruments from existing literature to ensure content validity, reliability, and contextual relevance for the Ghanaian tertiary student population. The GHQ-12 has been validated in various African university contexts, and in this study, it showed satisfactory internal reliability (Cronbach’s alpha = 0.81). No external financial support, sponsorship, or grants were received, ensuring the independence and objectivity of the research process and its findings.Author informationAuthors and AffiliationsDepartment of Educational Foundations, University of Education, Winneba (UEW), Winneba, West Africa, GhanaSimon NtumiDepartment of Interdisciplinary Studies, Akenten Appiah-Menka University of Skills Training and Entrepreneurial Development, West Africa, GhanaDaniel Gyapong NimoDepartment of Counselling Psychology, University of Education, Winneba (UEW), Winneba, West Africa, GhanaChristina AmmahBagabaga College of Education, Tamale, West Africa, GhanaBetty DonkorBia Lamplighter College of Education, Sefwi Debiso, West Africa, GhanaSheilla AgbenyoDepartment of Education, Komenda College of Education, Komenda, West Africa, GhanaHarriet Delali DekuSt.",
