      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 121
    },
    {
      "text": "Mediation was considered significant when the confidence interval for the indirect effect did not contain zero.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 122
    },
    {
      "text": "All statistical analyses were conducted at a 95% confidence level, and a p-value of less than 0.05 was considered statistically significant.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 123
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 4.2% of cases contained missing values on one or more study variables.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 124
    },
    {
      "text": "This suggests that the use of listwise deletion is unlikely to have introduced systematic bias, supporting the interpretive rigor of the analyses.Ethical considerationsThe study adhered strictly to ethical research standards throughout the planning, data collection, and reporting processes.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 125
    },
    {
      "text": "Prior to data collection, ethical clearance was sought and obtained from the Institutional Review Board (IRB) of the University of Education, Winneba with protocol number UEW/IRB/2025/027.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
