      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 126
    },
    {
      "text": "The IRB approval confirmed that the study posed minimal risk to participants and complied with institutional and international guidelines for research involving human subjects.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 127
    },
    {
      "text": "Participation in the study was entirely voluntary.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 128
    },
    {
      "text": "To ensure anonymity and protect participant confidentiality, no personally identifying information such as names, student ID numbers, phone numbers, or IP addresses was collected.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 129
    },
    {
      "text": "The survey platform, Google Forms, was configured to avoid capturing email addresses automatically.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 130
    },
    {
      "text": "Data were securely stored in a password-protected cloud drive accessible only to the core research team.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 131
    },
    {
      "text": "After the completion of data collection and analysis, the data were anonymized and archived following data management protocols to allow for transparency and reproducibility of findings.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
      "doi": "10.1038/s41598-026-40285-0",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 132
    },
    {
      "text": "Recognizing the sensitivity of some questions, particularly those related to depression and mental health, the research team included a debriefing page at the end of the survey.",
      "paperTitle": "Mental health and depression as mediators between social media use screen time and academic integrity among tertiary students in Ghana",
