      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 67
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher levels of adventurous play were also associated with lower internalising scores.",
      "paperTitle": "Are play and screen time associated with British preschoolers’ mental health? Cross-sectional findings from the British Preschool Children’s Play Survey",
      "doi": "10.1136/bmjopen-2025-105101",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 68
    },
    {
      "text": "No other significant associations were found between play and outcomes.View this table:View inlineView popupTable 3Associations between play, screen time and mental health outcomes in British preschool-aged children (n=1018)Educational screen time of 1–2 or >2 hours per day (vs <1 hour) was associated with poorer mental health outcomes in preschool-aged children.",
      "paperTitle": "Are play and screen time associated with British preschoolers’ mental health? Cross-sectional findings from the British Preschool Children’s Play Survey",
