    },
    {
      "text": "Error bar indicates 95% confidence interval.We conducted sensitivity analyses to examine whether using an adventure level of >3 (compared with >2) affected associations with mental health outcomes: adventurous play remained associated with both internalising and positive affect (online supplemental table 2).",
      "paperTitle": "Are play and screen time associated with British preschoolers’ mental health? Cross-sectional findings from the British Preschool Children’s Play Survey",
      "doi": "10.1136/bmjopen-2025-105101",
