0.1177/147470491100900212OpenUrlPubMed↵DaviesDSC,AthertonF,McBrideM,et al.UK chief medical officers’ physical activity guidelines.In:Department of health and social care.2019:1–65.↵HeskethKR,JanssenX.Movement behaviours and adherence to guidelines: perceptions of a sample of UK parents with children 0-18 months.Int J Behav Nutr Phys Act2022;19:58.doi:10.1186/s12966-022-01300-5OpenUrl↵HeskethKD,HinkleyT,CampbellKJ.Children’s physical activity and screen time: qualitative comparison of views of parents of infants and preschool children.Int J Behav Nutr Phys Act2012;9:152.doi:10.1186/1479-5868-9-152↵De DeckerE,De CraemerM,De BourdeaudhuijI,et al.Influencing factors of screen time in preschool children: an exploration of parents’ perceptions through focus groups in six European countries.Obes Rev2012;13 Suppl 1:75–84.doi:10.1111/j.1467-789X.2011.00961.xOpenUrl↵StiglicN,VinerRM.Effects of screentime on the health and well-being of children and adolescents: a systematic review of reviews.BMJ Open2019;9:e023191.doi:10.1136/bmjopen-2018-023191↵The Office of National Statistics.Census.2022.Available:https://www.ons.gov.uk/censusFootnotesContributorsHFD and KRH conceptualised the design of the study and developed the survey questions.",
