media on children’s intelligence while controlling for genetic differences in cognition and socioeconomic background.Sci Rep. (2022)12:7720. doi:10.1038/s41598-022-11341-2,Pubmed AbstractCrossRefGoogle Scholar15.Barajas-MartínezAIbarra-CoronadoESierra-VargasMPCruz-BautistaIAlmeda-ValdesPAguilar-SalinasCAet al.Physiological network from anthropometric and blood test biomarkers.Front Physiol. (2021)11:612598. doi:10.3389/fphys.2020.612598CrossRefGoogle Scholar16.GolbeckJ.Chapter 3 - network structure and measures. In:GolbeckJ, editor.Analyzing the social web.Boston:Morgan Kaufmann; (2013). Available online at:https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B9780124055315000031(Accessed December 24, 2025).Google Scholar17.BatushanskyAToubianaDFaitA.Correlation-based network generation, visualization, and analysis as a powerful tool in biological studies: a case study in Cancer cell metabolism.Biomed Res Int. (2016)2016:8313272. doi:10.1155/2016/8313272,Pubmed AbstractCrossRefGoogle Scholar18.ButtsC. T.:Sna: tools for social network analysis.R... - Google Académico. Available online at:https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?&journal=Sna%3A+Tools+for+Social+Network+Analysis+%28R+Package+Version+2%2E5%29&author=Butts+C.+T.&publication_year=2019(Accessed December 24, 2025).Google Scholar19.BorgattiSPEverettMG.A graph-theoretic perspective on centrality.Soc Netw. (2006)28:466–84. doi:10.1016/j.socnet.2005.11.005CrossRefGoogle Scholar20.ManujaRPattankarTPYadavannavarMCUdgiriRSManujaRPattankarTPet al.Impact of elevated screen time on school-age adolescents during the COVID-19 pandemic: an analytical study.Cureus. (2024)16:e64689.",
