      "text": "• Screen-use correlates differed by modality, underscoring the importance of distinguishing between gaming, social media, and film/TV use in adolescent research. Alcohol use, shorter sleep duration, smoking, higher psychosomatic symptoms, school absenteeism were associated with higher pooled screen time while being a female, living with both parents, and having physical activity were associated with lower pooled screen time. The correlates of pooled screen time and more especially shorter sleep duration, living with both parents, higher physical activity, and school absenteeism are important factors for moderating screen time adolescents.",
