      "text": "Excessive ST (≥6h/day) was associated with CMD in girls (PR=1.61; 95%CI: 1.44–1.80) and boys (PR=1.40; 95%CI: 1.15–1.72). A lack of PA combined with excessive ST increased CMD prevalence by 46% in girls and 72% in boys. The combined exposure to high ST and low PA further increased CMD, particularly among boys.",
