  "10.1109/iciss67859.2026.11454070": [
    {
      "text": "The growing rate of exposure to excessive screen time in children in India has also increased the demand of predictive models that can be used reliably to determine the patterns of behavior risks at an early age. This paper presents a proposal of an Enhanced Gradient-Based Optimizer combined with a Random Forest stacking ensemble to classify behavioral risk levels of the screen time behavior by utilizing a set of behavioral and demographic features together. It is a research based on an 8,742 records of children between the ages of 4 to 16 years, including 24 variables that determine the screen use habits, physical activities, sleep habits, academic variables, and the socio demographic variables. These results suggest that the suggested framework offers a strong and analytically justified framework of assessment of behavioral risk of screen time usage, and it could be potentially applicable to child health monitoring and intervention planning based on data.",
      "paperTitle": "Enhanced Gradient based Optimizer with Random Forest Stacking Ensemble for Predicting Screen Time Behavioral Patterns in Indian Children: A Hybrid Machine Learning Approach",
      "doi": "10.1109/iciss67859.2026.11454070",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "The systematic cleaning, normalization and encoding of data were applied and feature selection based on mutual information was done to drop the less discriminative features.",
      "paperTitle": "Enhanced Gradient based Optimizer with Random Forest Stacking Ensemble for Predicting Screen Time Behavioral Patterns in Indian Children: A Hybrid Machine Learning Approach",
      "doi": "10.1109/iciss67859.2026.11454070",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Synthetic Minority Over-sampling Technique was used to target the issue of class imbalance and allow equal learning opportunities in terms of risk category.",
      "paperTitle": "Enhanced Gradient based Optimizer with Random Forest Stacking Ensemble for Predicting Screen Time Behavioral Patterns in Indian Children: A Hybrid Machine Learning Approach",
      "doi": "10.1109/iciss67859.2026.11454070",
      "source": "openalex",
      "yearPublished": 2026,
      "chunk_index_in_doc": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed stacking model incorporates the use of Random Forest, Extra Trees, Gradient Boosting, and XGBoost as base learners and a Random Forest classifier as the meta learner.",
      "paperTitle": "Enhanced Gradient based Optimizer with Random Forest Stacking Ensemble for Predicting Screen Time Behavioral Patterns in Indian Children: A Hybrid Machine Learning Approach",
      "doi": "10.1109/iciss67859.2026.11454070",
